<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="realism-bands-v2" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip files-touched rows and callouts follow the sibling plan fragments' inline markup so the page renders them identically -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/realism-bands.json</summary><div class="pl-card">Schema version 2. Eleven new bands: 10 or more goals share 0 to 0.5%, sending-off share 8 to 22%, yellow cards per team 1.2 to 2.6, shots on target share 30 to 42%, goals per xG 0.85 to 1.15, passes per team 350 to 550, pass accuracy 75 to 88%, corners per team 3.5 to 6.5, throw-ins per match 35 to 55, goal kicks per match 12 to 22, goalless share 4 to 12%.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>content</td><td>+13 / -1</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/tactics.json</summary><div class="pl-card">Six formations are appended after the four shipped ones: 4-1-4-1, 4-4-1-1, 4-1-2-1-2, 3-4-3, 5-3-2 and 5-4-1. Indices 0 to 3 do not move.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>content</td><td>+96</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine-cli/src/report/mod.rs, bands.rs, compare.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The bands loader reads version 2 and refuses version 1. The equal suite adds eleven checks. The formations suite checks goals per match, the 10 or more goals share and the goalless share for each of 55 pairings. A check carries an optional pairing. The paired-run distance counts only the excess above the high end for a band whose low end is 0.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src/report</td><td>+265 / -54</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/calibrate/*, cli.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">A formations suite in --suite all: every unordered formation pair with mirrors, 1,000 matches each, the formation at home alternating. Both sides get their formation through MatchConfig::with_tactics. One warn line names each failing band. Events are written only for outlier matches when the measurement shows a gain.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src/calibrate</td><td>+154 / -19</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine/src/observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The match-stats record gains stats.throw_ins and stats.goal_kicks, copied from the counters the engine already keeps.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src/observe</td><td>+14</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> schemas/observability/match-stats and run-report</summary><div class="pl-card">The two new statistics are required on a success record. The run report accepts the formations suite, the new figures, the pairing field and the calib.formations list.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>schemas/observability</td><td>+90 / -3</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine-cli/tests, crates/engine tests</summary><div class="pl-card">A formations smoke run with 1 match per pairing, a stderr check for a failing band, the schema checks for the new keys, the pinned compare rows, the formation count, and the slow test on every band (red until realism-tuning).</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>tests</td><td>+75 / -18</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> .ai/observability.md, docs/reference, docs/how-to, content/README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The new keys, the bands with their sources, the formations suite and its run time, and the refusal of an old bands file.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>docs</td><td>+69 / -13</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>A full run takes over an hour (high).</strong> --suite all plays 57,000 matches: about 74 minutes per seed, and about 6 hours for the five-seed baseline. Every pairing plays 1,000 matches by the product owner's choice.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Expected red runs (medium).</strong> Calibration exits 2 and the ignored slow test fails until realism-tuning. The product owner accepted this.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Content hash moves (medium).</strong> New formations change tactics.json, so a snapshot saved before this slice is refused on resume. Implement re-derives every pinned hash on the record.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Band values from local sources (low).</strong> Seven values come from the design document's local Wyscout and StatsBomb outputs, not the document itself. content/README.md cites each one.</aside>
  </div>
